####

01: Teste ID                 --> Teste ID
02: seed_RL                  --> Seed for generating pseudorandom numbers - RL
03: load_factor              --> Multiplicative factor for load at all buses (e.g., 2.00 indicates that the load will be doubled)
04: gen_factor               --> Multiplicative factor for generation capacity at all generating stations (e.g., 2.00 indicates that the generating capacity will be doubled)
05: circuit_factor           --> Multiplicative factor for the capacity of all circuits, TLs and TRAFOS (e.g., 0.50 indicates that the capacities will be reduced by half)
------------------------------------- 
SL settings - Pretraining:
06: N_samples_PT             --> Number of samples
07: n_epochs_PT              --> Number of epochs
08: batch_size_PT            --> Batch size
09: lr_actor_PT              --> Learning rate - actor
10: lr_critic_PT             --> Learning rate - critic (baseline)
------------------------------------- 
RL settings:
11: n_episodes               --> number of episodes during the training using RL
								 * To evaluate a pure SL-GNN policy, consider using a lower number of episodes (e.g., 10).
12: batch_size_RL            --> batch sizes for training using RL
13: lr_actor_RL              --> learning rate - actor
14: lr_critic_RL             --> learning rate - critic (baseline)  
15: entropy_coef_RL          --> entropy coefficient (regularization)
16: ppo_epochs               --> number of epochs - PPO  
17: ppo_clip                 --> clip value - PPO
------------------------------------- 
GNNs settings:
18: hidden_dim_actor         --> number of hidden dimensions for actor GNN
19: n_heads_actor            --> number of heads for actor GNN
20: n_layers_actor           --> number of layers for actor GNN
21: hidden_dim_critic        --> number of hidden dimensions for critic GNN
22: n_heads_critic           --> number of heads for critic GNN
23: n_layers_critic          --> number of layers for critic GNN
24: std_min                  --> minimal value for standart deviation (exploration parameter)
25: std_max                  --> maximal value for standart deviation (exploration parameter)
26: dropout                  --> dropout rate
------------------------------------- 
MCS settings:
27: RA_crude_eval            --> Will a conventional NS-MCS be performed (AC-OPF-NS-MCS (benchmark))? (True or False)
28: RA_GNN_PT_eval           --> Will a SP-GNN (trained only via SL - SL-GNN-NS-MCS) be performed? (True or False)
								 * To evaluate a pure SL-GNN policy, consider the number of samples and epochs accordingly, and set this parameter to 'True'.
29: RA_GNN_RL_eval           --> Will a RL-GNN (RL-GNN-NS-MCS) be performed? (True or False)
								 * To evaluate a pure SL-GNN policy, set this parameter to 'False'.
30: samples_performance      --> Total of samples to performance analysis (statistics)